mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Pharmaceutics I is a foundational course for pharmacy majors that systematically introduces the basic theories and preparation techniques of drug dosage forms and pharmaceutical preparations. It covers common dosage forms such as liquid preparations, injections, eye drops, tablets, capsules, pills, powders, granules, suppositories, ointments, gels, films, and aerosols. The course focuses on the concepts, characteristics, formulation theories, prescription composition, preparation processes, and quality evaluation parameters of each dosage form, thereby helping students build a comprehensive knowledge framework in pharmaceutics.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
